// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/analog/sar_kick_net.t27 -- the SAR ADC comparator's clock-edge kick on the two top plates, derived: a 34-node capacitor network, the drivers' resistances, the comparator's charge pulse from charge tables, M1's fixed-step solve
; M4e-kick of the SAR ADC milestone (#10942, part of #10888 and #10818, epic #10486). sar_kick.t27 (#10941) MEASURED where the converter's decision offset comes from: when the comparator's clock rises, its
; input pair pushes charge into the two top plates VDP and VDN, they fall by 22.7 and 30.2 mV by clkc = 0.75 V, and the 7.5 mV between them is what the latch reads, because the N half's bottom plates are driven
; through one transmission gate more than the P half's. The kick was measured there, not derived. This file derives it, from the netlist, the PSP103 tables and ngspice measurements on committed decks, with no
; number fitted to a code or to a kick it predicts (FR-001).
; -
; THE CHAIN. (1) THE PULSE. The input pair (XM3, XM4: 36 sg13_lv_nmos W 1 um in parallel) has its gate on the plate, its source on the tail node net1 and its drain on ap (an). When clkc rises net1 falls from 0.65 V
; to 0.04 V and ap from 1.5 V to 0.05 V (sar_kick_edge.cir prints both, 67 samples 0.1 ns apart, the two gates on ideal sources). The gate charge Q_G(Vg, Vs, Vd) of one device at 50 C with the bulk on ground
; comes from three tables of 25 x 25 points on three gate levels (sar_kick_qg.cir: M3c's recipe with the comparator's bulk and temperature), read bilinearly by M3a's reader along the two waves: the gates take
; dQ_G(t) from the plates. At clkc = 0.75 V that is 26.93 fC from the tables against 26.90 fC that ngspice integrated from the gate current (0.1 percent); M3c's own table (bulk at the source, 27 C) gives 36.4 fC,
; 35 percent more, which is why a table of its own was made.
; (2) THE PLATES. Each half is a capacitor network: 63 units of 122.94 fF (sar_cdac.t27: 31 on the top plate through its bottom plates, 31 on net1 behind the one-unit bridge), 12 fF of the golden top level and the
; tracking switch on each top plate, and the pair's gate capacitance (dQ_G / dVg across the tables: 59 fF at the 0.1 V crossing, 110 fF averaged over the pulse by the charge each interval puts in, because the
; matrix of M1's step is one constant matrix). Each bottom plate is held by its driver. An IDLE bit's drivers are the two-port ngspice measured in sar_kick_cnode.cir: the tgate x2 to VCM (2586 ohm) and x11
; between Bit and Bit_n (2587 ohm), and the capacitances the devices add, 25.6, 12.8 and 3.2 fF at 100 MHz. A MOVED bit's P plate is held by DAC_control's inverter, whose on-resistance (1419 ohm nmos, 1870 ohm
; pmos) M3b's 50 C current tables give within 0.6 percent of ngspice's (sar_off_ron.cir), and its N plate by the inverter and one tgate more, at a rail one device again: twice that (sar_kick_cnode_moved.cir
; measures the moved bit's operating point and two-port: 1881 / 1428 ohm and 3772 / 2862 ohm, within 1 percent of those, and the capacitances its devices add, 50 and 41 fF at the P plate's node, 11 and 19 fF
; at the N plate's, 2 fF between, which the network takes). The tables cannot give the tgate at VCM: a table is made with the source and bulk together and the golden tgate's nmos has its source at 0.75 V over a
; grounded bulk, so they read it 30 percent too stiff (1813 against 2586 ohm; control 3). The network is 34 nodes: VDP, VDN, their two net1 nodes and three per bit (Bit_k, Bit_k_n, the P plate behind its series
; resistor). The pulse goes into both top plates. M1's own matrix derivation is capped at 5 unknowns, so M = A^-1 C/dt and N = A^-1 b of x' = M x + N u are derived here by Gauss-Jordan elimination with partial
; pivoting (the solve's residual is tested), and every step of the run is M1's `step` on their Q.24 words, called by name; it follows the f64 run of the same method to 1.2 uV. dt = 10 ps, converged (control 5).
; (3) THE DECISION. The latch does not read VDP - VDN at one instant. sar_kick_aperture.cir steps the gate of VDP by 1 mV at a time tau and reads the latch's output difference 4.8 ns after the 0.1 V crossing;
; the ratio to the response of a step before the edge is the share of the decision that the input still decides at tau: 1.00 until 3 ns after the crossing, 0.60 at 4.0 ns, 0.07 at 4.5 ns, 0 from 4.75 ns (20
; transients, linear in the step to 0.3 percent). The decision reads the change of VDP - VDN since the crossing weighted by those shares, plus the latch's own 0.153 mV (M4b-psp): the offset.
; -
; THE RESULT, first decision, every plate idle. ngspice: sar_kick.t27. A: the issue's model, one charge pulse for the pair. B: the extension the three gate-level tables allow, each plate's device taking the charge
; of its own gate level (0.742 V + D / 2 for VDP, - D / 2 for VDN, D the VDP - VDN of the experiment; the charge rises 81 fC per volt of gate), the offsets at the D the decision flips at (the fixed point
; d = -off: the measured flip is no input).
;   S1  the golden circuit, dVDP / dVDN at clkc 0.75 V      -22.7 / -30.2 mV    A -22.4 / -29.5 mV    1.3 / 2.0 percent (criterion 10)      B -22.3 / -29.7 mV   1.7 / 1.5 percent
;   S2  both halves ideal, dVDP = dVDN                      -6.87 / -6.88 mV    A -6.71 / -6.71 mV    2.2 percent (5), differ 0 (0.1 mV)     B -6.71 / -6.72 mV   2.3 percent
;       (the network is then a capacitor divider: the closed form agrees to 0.5 percent)
;   S3  N half ideal, dVDP - dVDN                           -20.5 mV            A -19.1 mV            6.6 percent (15)                       B -19.9 mV           2.6 percent
;       P half ideal                                        +35.9 mV            A +33.0 mV            8.1 percent (15)                       B +35.0 mV           2.7 percent
;   S4  P plates behind 1300 / 2592 / 3900 ohm, offset      +4.09 / -0.89 / -4.19 mV   A +4.06 / -0.55 / -4.77 mV (within 0.6 mV, 1)    B +4.19 / -0.57 / -4.95 mV
;       it crosses the latch's 0.153 mV at                  2320 ohm            A 2386 ohm (asked 2200 .. 2450)
;   the seven offsets (SC 2, within 1 mV): ngspice          base 9.42, ideal switches 9.19, comparator isolated 0.03, N ideal -25.79, P ideal +43.87, both ideal 0.27, 2592 ohm -0.89
;                                                       A   9.34, 9.34 (the switch is not in the network), 0.15 (no pulse: the latch's own), -24.86, +43.03, 0.15, -0.55: all within 1 mV
;                                                       B   9.60, 9.60, 0.15, -25.71, +45.02, 0.16, -0.57: the P half ideal row is 1.15 mV above ngspice's, 0.15 mV past the 1 mV; the rest within 0.4 mV
;   the order P ideal > golden > symmetric = comparator isolated > N ideal holds in both; the signs and sizes are the measurement's. B is closer on every kick (the three differentials 0.8, 2.6, 2.7 percent against
;   4.1, 6.6, 8.1) and one row further on the offset: the offset is the kick read through the aperture, and the model's ratio of the one to the other is 1.30 against ngspice's 1.26. A is the issue's model and
;   the default of everything below; B is stated beside it wherever it differs.
; -
; THE CONTROLS, each a test that passes by seeing the failure:
;   1. no pulse: the plates stay put and the offset is the latch's 0.153 mV.
;   2. M3c's table for the pulse (35 percent more charge): the plates fall 21 percent too far, S1 fails its 10 percent.
;   3. the tgate from M3b's tables (no body effect, 1.43 times too stiff a drive): S1 fails by 17 and 19 percent, the base offset is 2 mV low.
;   4. the idle bit's two-port capacitances left out: the one-half-ideal rows move by 1.7 and 2.7 mV, the 2592 ohm row misses ngspice's by 1.02 mV.
;   5. dt = 100 ps (one step per sample): the one-half-ideal rows move by 0.55 and 0.87 mV and miss the 1 mV criterion; dt = 5 ps moves them by 0.03 mV.
;   6. (late decisions) the first decision's edge and aperture, as the first lane read them: 7.09, 7.09, 6.77, 6.77 mV, the first conversion's tenth 0.43 mV off; the late edge with the first decision's
;      aperture: 6.98, 7.01, 6.80, 6.77 (the aperture's timing is worth 0.1 to 0.2 mV: 0.6 mV per 0.1 ns); the bits' capacitances left out: +0.11, +0.11, +0.05, +0.05 mV; the first conversion's plates under the
;      second's edge and aperture, and the reverse: 0.3 mV from the plates that belong to them.
; -
; THE LATE DECISIONS (S5). The converter's codes are decided by the last decisions (sar_kick.t27: 6.66 and 6.90 mV at decisions 9 and 10, from 28 decisions each). The first lane read them with the first
; decision's pulse and aperture and missed by 0.2 to 0.6 mV, for want of the late decision's own edge. sar_kick_late.cir reads the golden sine's own clock edge at its tenth and eleventh decisions (net1 38 to 46 mV
; below the first decision's at the window start, 0.614 and 0.622 V against 0.660 V; the pair takes 27.2 to 27.6 fC between 0.1 V and 0.75 V, its gate capacitance 111 to 113 fF; the plates' common mode 0.741 V in
; the first conversion, 0.749 V in the second); sar_kick_late_aperture.cir measures the aperture there (the latch has 0.68 and 0.71 of the first decision's gain at the read instant and its share closes earlier:
; 0.555 at 4.0 ns against 0.601); sar_kick_cnode_moved.cir the moved bit. The decision with nine (ten) plates moved is the network with those plates held by their inverters (the P plate down for a decision of
; 1 and up for 0, from the sine's own decisions, the N plate the other way behind the inverter and the tgate) and the idle one by its two-port, driven by its own edge and aperture. Offsets in mV:
;                                    A one pulse    B own gate levels    measured (sar_kick.t27)
;   first conversion, decision 9     6.83           7.00                 6.658 +- 0.05, one threshold for all 28 paths
;   first conversion, decision 10    6.86           7.08                 6.895, 6.85 to 7.06 by the bit path
;   second conversion, decision 9    6.63           6.90                 6.658
;   second conversion, decision 10   6.60           6.82                 6.895
;   within the issue's 0.2 mV        3 of 4         2 of 4
; S5 is NOT met, by either: A misses the second conversion's decision 10 by 0.29 mV (and sits 0.25 mV under the lowest the paths allow), B the two decisions 9 by 0.34 and 0.24 mV. The mean of A's four,
; 6.731 mV, is 0.045 mV under the 6.776 the converter model takes; sar_adc.t27 is NOT switched to the derived value (the success criterion asks for S5 first) and is untouched. What the network does not have, and
; the next gap: (1) the bit path. The measured offset at decision 9 is one number over all 28 paths (0.05 mV); the network's two paths are 0.2 mV apart and its plates under the other path's edge 0.3 mV: the
; up and down drives of a moved plate (1881 and 1428 ohm for the P plate, 3772 and 2862 for the N plate) matter more in the model than in the circuit, where the inverter's output sits within tens of
; millivolts of its rail through the kick and the tables read it at Vds -> 0. (2) decision 10 against 9: the measured offset is 0.24 mV higher at the tenth, the network's the same to 0.03 mV (the one-unit plate
; that moves in between). A reading of the in-situ moved bit's drive during the kick (not at 10 mV) and of the plate's own settling is the experiment that would separate them.
; -
; S5, SECOND LANE (decks sar_kick_plates.cir and sar_kick_late_aperture.cir with sar_which 2 and 3; the last three tests). The two named gaps were read in ngspice at the decisions themselves.
;   THE PULSE IS RIGHT. The gate current of each plate's 36 devices, integrated from the 0.1 V to the 0.75 V crossing of the sine run, is 25.1 to 25.6 fC; the three charge tables read at the plate's own
;   gate voltage give it to 0.1 to 0.6 percent (test: within 1.5); the single pulse (gates held at 0.742 V) is 27.2 to 27.6 fC, 7 to 10 percent more, and the network's gate capacitance takes it back.
;   GAP 2 IS NOT A CIRCUIT EFFECT. ngspice's own balance (the latch's margin over its slope in the input: the LINEAR rows) is 6.984 mV at decision 9 and 6.991 at decision 10 of the first conversion,
;   6.771 and 6.769 of the second: one number per conversion (7 and 3 uV apart), and within 0.03 mV on all eight DC conversions on five bit paths. The network's 10 - 9 is +0.033 and -0.028 mV. The 0.24 mV
;   between the pooled thresholds (6.658, 6.895) is the mix of paths each was bracketed on: the path 793 balances at 7.15 to 7.17 mV at both decisions, the paths 1014, 502 and 470 at 6.68 to 6.70.
;   GAP 1 IS REAL AND THE NETWORK HAS MOST OF IT. The balance depends on the bit path by 0.48 mV (6.68 to 7.17 mV on five paths; the sine's two 6.77 and 6.99): the network has the same order and 0.345
;   mV of the spread (71 percent). It is below ngspice's balance on every path by 0.10 to 0.29 mV: 0.13 to 0.17 mV at the sine's four decisions, so all four are within the issue's 0.2 mV of ngspice's own
;   offset at that decision (test); against the pooled thresholds S5 is still 3 of 4 (the miss above). On the DC paths 0.10 to 0.29 mV low is not within 0.2.
;   NOT CLOSED, what the measurements say is missing. (a) A part that does not depend on the path: ngspice's own plate waves read through the same aperture give 0.14 to 0.18 mV less than its balance at
;   the five decisions that sit at balance (margin under 4 mV): the latch's own offset in the converter is about 0.31 mV, not the 0.153 mV of its isolated test. The cause is not found; the common mode is
;   not excluded: stepping both gates together moves the margin by +0.70, +0.37, +0.30 and +0.59 mV per mV at the windows 1, 2, 4 and 5 (1.2 to 2.8 percent of the differential slope, at the
;   pre-edge instant; sar_part 3), the same sign for a falling common mode as a lower offset, so by itself it does not give the missing +0.15 mV; its aperture in time is not measured. (b) The gate capacitance is not constant: 59 fF until 1.5 ns after the crossing, 130 to 150 fF from 3 to 4.5 ns
;   (the tables), the network carries the pulse-weighted 112.8 fF. With it varying (a throwaway script outside this file, one matrix per 1.1 ns) the network's twenty bottom-plate nodes follow ngspice's
;   to 0.1 to 0.3 mV and the offset read from the network equals the one read from ngspice's own waves to 0.08 mV (6.66, 6.73, 6.56, 6.49 mV), which lowers the four by 0.1 to 0.17 mV, away from the balance:
;   the first decision's rows (S1 to S4, edge deck) get 3 to 5 percent too small a kick with it, so it is not taken here. (c) The kick depends on D more than the network says: ngspice's differential kick
;   grows 0.10 mV per mV of D below the flip (the plates' gates 0.5 mV apart each), the network's 0.02 to 0.05 (model B).
; -
; WHAT IS NOT DERIVED (FR-003). With ideal plates the first plate step reads a top-plate load Cp of 0.582 units of the 9 um capacitor; the network's own is the explicit 12 fF plus the pair's gate capacitance at
; the pre-edge bias from the tables, 59.2 fF: 0.579 units, within 1 percent, a test. The golden circuit reads 0.647 and the P plates behind 1300, 2592 and 3900 ohm read 0.62, 0.69 and 0.85, and a raised and a lowered P
; plate differ by 2.85 mV (sar_kick.t27). The network has the mechanism (the biggest plate settles later the softer its driver, and the N half's, one tgate softer, later still; the raised case's slowest path is 2838
; ohm and the lowered case's 3740, which gives the sign of the 2.85 mV, not tested here) and no number for it: the step is read a time after the plate moves that the pinned data do not hold (the inverter's own
; switching, the time to the second clkc edge). It is the next gap.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. The pinned data are the numbers the decks printed (six folds); the tables' pulse is ngspice's to 0.1 percent and the table of M3c is not; the drivers' resistances are the tables' and the
; measured two-ports', within the stated percent of ngspice's own measurements; the network's solve is a solve and M1's words follow the f64 run to 1.2 uV; with ideal plates the network is the capacitor divider;
; the derived kicks are within the issue's tolerances of ngspice's (S1 to S4) and the seven first-decision offsets within 1 mV, in the measured order; the controls fail the way they are said to; the late decisions
; are derived with their own edge and aperture to 0.17, 0.03, 0.03 and 0.29 mV (A), and S5's miss is pinned with its numbers.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. Nothing about speed, power, noise, mismatch, another corner or another temperature, and nothing about decks beyond the numbers pinned here: this file runs no ngspice. S1 to S4 read the first
; decision's edge (ideal gate sources, plates settled for 14 ns), which is what the offsets were measured on; the tracking switch's own charge injection is not in the network (the ideal-switch row is the base row:
; ngspice found the two 0.23 mV apart); the switch's off-state junction capacitance (about 0.3 fF) is not in the 12 fF; for A the gate charge is read at one gate level for both plates (B reads each at its own).
; The windows of the sine run's first decisions are pinned for their D (a check of the run) and one test: window 0 (rise 1, plates 31 mV apart, read with the table at one gate level for both: 9.97 mV against
; the edge deck's 9.34), window 3 (rise 12, plates 269 mV apart, beyond the tables' gate range) not at all.
; ASCII only, English only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module AnalogSarKickNet;

use analog::linear::{step, q_sm, sm_f64, fabs64, fold, SCALE};
use analog::mos_table::{idf};
use analog::mos_psp103_50c_data::{TT50_N, TT50_P};
use analog::mos_psp103_data::{TT_QG_N, fold_arr};
use analog::sar_cdac::{PLATES, UNITS, SIDE};
use analog::sar_kick::{V_BASE, V_IDEALSW, V_NOKICK, V_PLATES, V_NPLATE, V_PPLATE, LATCH_FLIP_V, KICK_P, KICK_N, FLIP_LO, RS_LO, RS_OHM, RON_TG, RON_INVP, RON_INVN, NRS, first_off, kick_diff, rs_off, rs_zero_ohm, cp_of_step, step_mean, late_thr, off_late_v, DEC_D, LD_BIT, RS_STEP_UP, RS_STEP_DN, STEP_UP, STEP_DN};

pub const KIND : str = "analog-cell";
pub const ID : str = "analog/sar_kick_net";
pub const REFERENCE : str = "uberWAVE wp2-parser/golden/top.spice (read at run time, GPL-2.0, not vendored); specs/analog/decks/sar_kick_*.cir";

; --- the units of the network ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Time in ns, capacitance in fF, charge in fC, resistance in ohm, voltage in V. Then a conductance in microsiemens is 1.0e6 / R and C / dt is in microsiemens too,
; a current in fC / ns is in microamperes, and (G + C / dt) x = ... is in volts. The unknowns are the node voltages as deviations from the pre-edge state.

/// Nodes of the network: the two top plates and their two net1 nodes, then three per bottom plate (Bit_k, Bit_k_n, the P plate behind its series resistor).
pub const NMAX : usize = 34;
pub const NSQ : usize = 1156;
/// The work matrix [A | C / dt | b]: NMAX rows of 2 NMAX + 1 columns.
pub const WA : usize = 69;
pub const NAUG : usize = 2346;
/// The ground, as a node index.
pub const GND : usize = 99;
/// A conductance that joins two nodes that are one node (1 mOhm), microsiemens.
pub const G_SHORT : f64 = 1000000000.0;

/// One cap_cmim unit (9 um x 9 um), fF (M4c, sar_switch.t27: 122.94 fF at 9 x 9).
pub const C_UNIT_FF : f64 = 122.94;
/// What the golden netlist hangs on each top plate besides the DAC and the comparator: C3 + C5 (C4 + C6) of the top level and C2 of the tracking switch, 4 fF each.
pub const C_EXPLICIT_FF : f64 = 12.0;
/// The input pair XM3, XM4 is 36 sg13_lv_nmos W 1.0 um in parallel.
pub const M_PAIR : f64 = 36.0;
/// One gate-charge table unit in fC: 500 fF * 2^-24 V.
pub const QG_UNIT_FC : f64 = 0.0000298023223876953125;
/// The gate step between the three charge tables, V, and the level of the middle one.
pub const QG_DVG : f64 = 0.05;
pub const VG_PLATES : f64 = 0.742;
/// The gate step between neighbouring charge tables, V.
pub const QG_DVG_STEP : f64 = 0.025;

/// Drive modes of a bottom plate, P half and N half alike.
pub const DR_IDLE : u8 = 0;
pub const DR_UP : u8 = 1;
pub const DR_DOWN : u8 = 2;
pub const DR_IDEAL : u8 = 3;
pub const DR_MIRROR : u8 = 4;

/// The waveform: 67 samples, 0.1 ns apart from 97.8 ns; clkc crosses 0.1 V at 99.3069 ns (sample 15.069) and 0.75 V at 103.118 ns (sample 53.18).
pub const NS : usize = 67;
pub const SAMPLE_NS : f64 = 0.1;
pub const T0_NS : f64 = 97.8;
pub const T01_NS : f64 = 99.3069;
pub const T075_NS : f64 = 103.118;
pub const T01_K : f64 = 15.069;
pub const T075_K : f64 = 53.18;
/// Steps of the network per sample: 10, so dt = 10 ps.
pub const SUB : usize = 10;

; --- BEGIN PINNED DATA (ngspice-47 + PSP103, IHP-Open-PDK 21133f21, mos_tt, 50 C; the decks specs/analog/decks/sar_kick_*.cir, read 2026-10-19) ----------------------
